Show power draw / intake instead of the plug icon

Replace the plug icon at the left of the bottom panel with the battery's current
power in whole watts, drawn in the existing small LCD font, with a "W" and a sign
underneath: '-' draining the battery, '+' charging, '=' on AC with the battery idle.
The power is read from the kernel's power_supply sysfs (power_now, or
current_now * voltage_now). When it is not reported the original plug icon is
drawn, as before.

Applies to Debian's wmbattery 2.56-1 (apply with: patch -p1).
